My desired use case would be having a script which stores references to other scripts and calls events on those scripts based on if they have said events.
It would go:
```
for (each script in the array) {
    if (event is exposed on other script) {
        run additional internal calculations;
        call event on other script;
    }
}
```
I do not want to arbitrarily run the internal calculations for EVERY script, only for those that I know are expecting the event to be called. 
Something simple like `public bool hasCustomEvent(string name)`, including its UGraph equivalent, would be perfect.

ShuffleArray sometimes causes "Index was outside the bounds of the array" exception with a very low probability. And it halts the UdonBehavior.
There was [an explanation of ShuffleArray](https://discord.com/channels/189511567539306508/449386885299830794/848015204729880576) on the main discord. If this is actual source code, the IndexOutOfRangeException could happen. Because `Random.value` range is "0.0 [inclusive] and 1.0 [inclusive]" (from [API reference](https://docs.unity3d.com/2019.4/Documentation/ScriptReference/Random-value.html)). So if `Random.value` returns `1.0`,  `int r` becomes `n` that is out of the range.
I think straight forward implementation of [Fisher–Yates shuffle](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fisher%E2%80%93Yates_shuffle) will fix this issue like this:
```
public static void ShuffleArray<T>(T[] array)
{
    int n = array.Length;
    for (int i = 0; i <= n - 2; i++)
    {
        int r = Random.Range(i, n);
        T t = array[r];
        array[r] = array[i];
        array[i] = t;
    }
}
```
Note: ureishi-san originally [found this issue](https://twitter.com/aivrc/status/1455088819405942785). What a great job again!

